Hi Jelle,

   Sorry for the late reply. Well, McCulloch's calibration can be interpreted as a probability between 0.5 and 1. In his calibration, a KL between a density P and a density Q for some random variable is equal to to a KL value between a Bernouilli distribution with probability (parameter) 1/2 and one with parameter q. If q is close to 1/2, this means that P and Q are as close to each other as B(1/2) and B(q). I know that this doesn't really solve your problem, but let me put together a comparison of t.tests, as you did, and the KLDC values and we can discuss them.

    Best,

  Fernando



